Subject: [PATCH] agent: support standalone backhaul STA radio ownership

Read optional AP and STA endpoints from the existing stock UCI radio sections.
Resolve a standalone STA's stable RUID and AP capabilities from the actual
physical device and permanent MAC, without creating an AP interface. Retain
per-radio M1 and accept only authenticated Controller TearDown for its zero-BSS
policy; an AP request remains a policy failure in the existing retry state.

Keep AP managers and monitors attached only to real AP endpoints. Route STA
onboarding, recovery and WPS through the existing backhaul owner, and decline
AP channel/scan operations on the dedicated uplink. Preserve ordinary AP-only
and AP+STA APIs and native UCI/supplicant ownership.

